# Controls what `gcloud run deploy --source .` uploads as the Cloud Build
# source bundle. Without this file, gcloud auto-generates one from
# .gitignore -- which excludes `data/` and `models/` wholesale (correctly,
# for git). Applied to a Cloud Build upload, that same exclusion silently
# drops the model artifact and marts the Dockerfile needs to COPY,
# producing a build failure one step later ("stat models: file does not
# exist") that looks unrelated to this file entirely. This file exists
# specifically to stop that inheritance -- everything it doesn't list is
# uploaded, including the gitignored-but-present models/ and
# data/03_marts/ the Dockerfile requires.
#
# .dockerignore still governs the actual `docker build` context on top of
# whatever this file lets through -- the two are deliberately kept in
# sync for the paths that matter (see that file's own comments).

.git/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Everything under data/ except what the Dockerfile actually needs:
# data/03_marts/ and feature_engineered_data.parquet. The raw/interim
# files are 1GB+ and irrelevant to the API image.
#
# NOTE: unlike .dockerignore, this can't exclude the whole
# data/02_processed/ directory and then `!`-negate one file back in --
# gcloudignore follows strict .gitignore semantics, where a negation
# cannot re-include a file whose parent directory was already excluded
# (verified: `gcloud meta list-files-for-upload` silently dropped the
# file with that approach). So the other two files in that directory are
# excluded individually instead.
data/00_raw/
data/01_interim/
data/02_processed/canonical_products_e5.parquet
data/02_processed/canonical_products_e5.parquet.manifest.json
data/02_processed/anomalies_flagged.parquet
data/03_external/
data/_run_reports/

frontend/
dashboard/
notebooks/
tests/
docs/
plots/
scripts/
site/
